    <!--
      Payment error dialog.

      THESE TWO STRINGS TOOK ARGUMENTS THEY HAD NO PLACEHOLDERS FOR, so `String.format` dropped
      both of them and the dialog said «Платёж не прошёл» and nothing else — for every failure,
      identically. Lint has been reporting it as StringFormatInvalid ×4
      (AccountFragment / BuyTariffActivity); the owner is testing payments with real money, and an
      error that cannot tell a declined card from a dead gateway costs him the diagnosis every time.

      They carry their arguments now:
        %1$s — the code, for quoting to support («402», «timeout», «network»);
        %2$s — the backend's own sanitised reason, when it sent one.

      This does NOT reopen copy law 9.4. The reason still leads with what the user can DO, the raw
      body is never dumped, and a failure with no reason still reads as a sentence rather than as a
      status line. What changed is that the dialog stopped withholding the one fact that identifies
      the failure.
    -->
    <!-- The label a money button wears while its charge is in flight. One control, one word,
         both billing surfaces — a control that is working says so, and stops taking taps (D10). -->
    <string name="account_pay_in_progress">Оплата…</string>

    <string name="account_payment_error_title">Ошибка оплаты</string>
    <string name="account_payment_error_body">Платёж не прошёл: %2$s\n\nПопробуйте другой способ оплаты. Код: %1$s</string>
    <string name="account_payment_error_body_nodetail">Платёж не прошёл. Попробуйте другой способ оплаты.\n\nКод: %1$s</string>

